TTYCHATTER.NCURSES(1)        User Commands        TTYCHATTER.NCURSES(1)

NAME
    ttychatter.ncurses - full-screen terminal chat client for OpenRouter

SYNOPSIS
    ttychatter.ncurses
    ttychatter.ncurses <session_name>
    ttychatter.ncurses --resume <session|session.log|/path/session.log>
    ttychatter.ncurses --list
    ttychatter.ncurses --models
    ttychatter.ncurses --update-models
    ttychatter.ncurses --test-model <model_id>
    ttychatter.ncurses --doctor
    ttychatter.ncurses --demo
    ttychatter.ncurses --version
    ttychatter.ncurses --loopback-file <path>
    ttychatter.ncurses --help

DESCRIPTION
    ttychatter.ncurses is the primary full-screen terminal interface for the
    ttychatter project. It is designed to make browser interfaces unnecessary
    for text-message-style AI work from a terminal. It talks to OpenRouter by
    default, uses cached model metadata, stores sessions as plain text logs,
    and saves long code blocks as local attachments.

LOOPBACK OUTPUT
    ttychatter.ncurses --loopback-file <path>
        Appends each AI response to the named file while the full-screen
        ncurses interface remains active.

        The ncurses client owns the terminal display, so direct stdout piping
        of the full-screen interface is not recommended. File-based loopback
        is the curses-safe way to let another process consume responses.

DEMO MODE
    --demo runs ttychatter.ncurses without OpenRouter network calls.

    Demo mode supplies local model metadata and local AI responses. It is
    intended for release-candidate testing, UI testing, model-browser testing,
    attachment extraction testing, session testing, and first-time exploration
    without spending OpenRouter credits or sending fake prompts to
    openrouter/free.

    In demo mode the header displays a visible marker:

        ttychatter.ncurses ~DEMO~

    In demo mode:
        - no OpenRouter API key is required
        - no chat-completions request is made
        - the model list comes from local demo rows
        - model tests return local demo responses
        - the demo response includes short and long code blocks so attachment
          extraction can be tested without provider traffic

LIVE REQUEST CONFIRMATION
    When CONFIRM_LIVE_SEND is enabled, the first non-demo send asks for
    confirmation before making a real OpenRouter chat request.

    This exists because ttychatter has many UI features that can be tested
    offline. Users who are trying menus, model browsers, or attachment handling
    should use --demo when they do not intend to spend provider requests.

USAGE
    First run with a real provider:
        ttychatter.ncurses
        Press F3 to enter an OpenRouter API key.
        Press F2 to use/update the cached model list or enter a model ID.

    Local no-network test run:
        ttychatter.ncurses --demo

    Resume with shell tab completion:
        ttychatter.ncurses --resume notes.log
        ttychatter.ncurses --resume /path/to/notes.log

CONTROLS
    F1        Help / command menu.
    F2        Model menu and model browser.
    F3        API key tools.
    F4        Sessions: switch, new chat, rename, delete.
    F5        Options.
    F6        Memory.
    F7        Files / attachments.
    F8        External editor.
    F9        Credits.
    F10       Quit.

    Enter     Sends by default when SEND_INPUT=enter.
    Ctrl+G    Reliable alternate send key.
    j/k       Move in menus, lists, model browser, memory, files, and editor
              screens.

MODEL BROWSER
    The model browser is table-like. It supports typed search, favorites,
    metadata filters, model tests, and sorting. Cached model lists are preferred.
    Updating the model list contacts OpenRouter only after confirmation.

    Keys inside the browser:
        /       Search by typed string.
        b       Toggle favorite/bookmark for the highlighted model.
        o       Cycle model sort method forward.
        O       Cycle model sort method backward.
        f       Open model filter/options screen.
        t       Test highlighted model.
        i       Show model metadata.
        s       Save highlighted model to config.
        Enter   Activate highlighted model for the current run.
        j/k     Move down/up.

API KEY STORAGE
    API keys can come from several places. The preferred order is:

        1. OPENROUTER_API_KEY environment variable
        2. TTYCHATTER_API_KEY environment variable
        3. OPENROUTER_API_KEY or API_KEY in config
        4. GPG-encrypted api-key.gpg file
        5. F3 runtime API-key entry

    Optional encrypted storage uses an external gpg command. The default file is:

        ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/api-key.gpg

    A custom encrypted-key file can be configured with:

        API_KEY_GPG_FILE=/path/to/api-key.gpg

    The program never prints the decrypted key. The --doctor screen reports
    whether gpg exists and whether the encrypted key file exists, but it does
    not display secret values.

CONFIGURATION
    Config file:
        ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/config

    Important keys:
        OPENROUTER_API_KEY
        TTYCHATTER_API_KEY
        API_KEY_GPG_FILE
        CONFIRM_LIVE_SEND=1|0
        MODEL
        DEMO_MODE=1|0
        SEND_INPUT=enter|ctrl_g
        PROMPT_SESSION_NAME=1|0
        CONTEXT_TURNS
        SESSION_DIR
        ATTACHMENT_DIR
        MODEL_CACHE_FILE
        CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES
        MODEL_FILTER_CHAT_COMPLETIONS
        MODEL_FILTER_REQUIRE_TOKENS
        MODEL_FILTER_HIDE_PREVIEW
        MODEL_MIN_INPUT_TOKENS
        MODEL_MIN_OUTPUT_TOKENS
        MODEL_SORT_ORDER
            Sort order used by the model browser. Common values include
            favorites, api, name, display, input-desc, and output-desc.

DEFAULT DIRECTORIES
    config:      ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/config
    sessions:    ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions/
    attachments: ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/attachments/
    cache:       ~/.cache/ttychatter/openrouter/models.json

ATTACHMENTS
    Short fenced code blocks remain inline. Long fenced code blocks are saved
    into ATTACHMENT_DIR once they meet CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES.

LIMITATIONS
    Media support depends on OpenRouter model capability. Terminal mouse and
    key behavior depend on terminal emulator support. Demo mode is local and
    proves the ttychatter UI path, not provider quality. Ctrl+Enter is not
    documented as a primary send key because many terminal emulators do not
    report it distinctly from Enter.

VERSION
    ttychatter.ncurses version 0.13.0
